{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484836-what-on-earth-is-avatar-8","id":1484836,"title":"What on Earth is Avatar 8???","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-23T19:39:12-07:00","id":1484836,"title":"What on Earth is Avatar 8???","content":"For some reason I had never noticed that Voormas had this background, I always thought it was capped at 5! What is that supposed to mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T20:17:54-07:00","id":1484837,"title":"","content":"It means he is old and extremely powerful. (more detailed answer probably depends on which edition)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T21:00:16-07:00","id":1484838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484836-what-on-earth-is-avatar-8?p=1484837#post1484837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It means he is old and extremely powerful. (more detailed answer probably depends on which edition)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Surely, but the thing is, I don't even know what is that supposed to mean by the rules. I don't remember reading rules for Avatar above 5 anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T21:43:34-07:00","id":1484842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484836-what-on-earth-is-avatar-8?p=1484838#post1484838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Surely, but the thing is, I don't even know what is that supposed to mean by the rules. I don't remember reading rules for Avatar above 5 anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless the M20 books have something about it, I can't find anything. (You would think Masters of the Art would have had them, but no. \ud83e\udd28)<br /> <br /> My off the cuff suggestion would be that the cap for those sort of arcane metaphysics backgrounds (Avatar, Arcane, Familiar, etc.) be equal to the character's Arete rating, or if you wish, one rank higher. (So a character with Arete 5 could have Avatar 5 or 6, depending on your preferences.) In the case of Avatar, it means the baseline quintessence for the character continues to go up. Maybe +2 at ranks six and seven, +3 at ranks eight and nine. (I would say +5 at rank ten, but at that level you are more of a plot device than a character.)<br /> <br /> So a character with Avatar 8 would always stabilize at a minimum quintessence pool of 12. <br /> <br /> If you want to make it more powerful, you can raise the cap on how much quintessence they can spend per turn to lower magic(k) roll difficulty. Three points per turn at rank six and seven, and four points at rank eight and nine. (This does exceed the -3 difficulty per roll rule, but that may be one of the perks of archmage-dom, or it may have to be spread across multiple castings going on at a single time.)<br /> <br /> All of this is just stuff I am pulling out of my ear, based entirely on the 2nd ed core book I have handy. I'm not sure how well - if at all - it would translate to other editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T21:59:37-07:00","id":1484843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to make it more powerful, you can raise the cap on how much quintessence they can spend per turn to lower magic(k) roll difficulty. Three points per turn at rank six and seven, and four points at rank eight and nine. (This does exceed the -3 difficulty per roll rule, but that may be one of the perks of archmage-dom, or it may have to be spread across multiple castings going on at a single time.) </div> </div> </div>That seems interesting, I thought about using something similar, in the sense that using how much you can spend per turn/store by avatar 5, but increased (and also, how much you need). I liked the idea of going beyond the cap of -3 dfficulty to showcase the archmage's power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}